    networkServiceDesc.doc = "Reports the role of this process in a networked game, and joins, hosts and leaves matches.\012\012Use `Authority` to decide whether this machine makes gameplay decisions: `if NetworkService.Authority then`. A single-player game is also an authority, so the same code works with and without networking.\012\012`Join`, `Host` and `Disconnect` change the role at run time, at a safe point between two ticks, and `State` reports the current stage. `Authority` can change during a run: it becomes false after joining and true again after leaving. Code that runs for the whole game should listen for changes to `State` instead of reading `Authority` once.\012\012The command-line flags `--host`, `--serve` and `--join=` make the same calls before the first tick. `--serve` is the only way to run a dedicated server.";
