    remoteEventDesc.super = instanceClass;
    remoteEventDesc.flags = ClassFlags::None;
    remoteEventDesc.defaultName = atoms.intern("RemoteEvent");
    remoteEventDesc.doc = "Sends messages between machines in a multiplayer game: \"I bought the sword\" from a client to the server, or \"the round starts\" from the server to every client. Create it on the authority, for example in a `Folder` under `Workspace`. It replicates to every client like any instance, and a client finds it with `WaitForChild`.\012\012The authority identifies the sender of a message from the connection, not from the message's contents, so a client cannot send a message as another client. A client should report what it did; the authority decides what happened.\012\012Arguments can be nil, booleans, numbers, strings, buffers, vectors, `Color3`, `CFrame`, `Vector2`, `UDim`, `UDim2`, enum items, instances, and tables of these up to eight levels deep. An instance arrives as the receiver's own copy of it, or as nil if the receiver does not have it. A call raises an error for a function, a thread or a table that contains itself, and for a message larger than 64 KiB.\012\012The same script works in single-player, when hosting and when connected. On an authority, `FireServer` fires that machine's own `ServerReceived` with its local player, and a host's messages to its own player fire its own `ClientReceived`. Messages are reliable. Their events fire at the start of the tick after they arrive.";
