    unreliableRemoteEventDesc.super = instanceClass;
    unreliableRemoteEventDesc.flags = ClassFlags::None;
    unreliableRemoteEventDesc.defaultName = atoms.intern("UnreliableRemoteEvent");
    unreliableRemoteEventDesc.doc = "A `RemoteEvent` for data that is sent many times per second and replaced each time. Use it for the positions of a horde, the direction a player aims in or a boss's health, and never for anything that must arrive.\012\012A message is sent once and can be lost. It is not sent again, so a lost message delays nothing else, whereas a lost reliable message makes every later reliable message wait for it.\012\012The newest message wins. A message that arrives after a later one is dropped instead of being delivered late, across all of the game's unreliable events, so a script never receives a message older than one it already received.\012\012A message to a machine that does not have the event yet, or where no handler is connected, is dropped.\012\012The arguments are limited to 16 KiB; a larger message raises an error at the call. A message larger than about 1 KB is sent in several packets and is lost entirely if any of them is, so large messages are lost more often. Send small messages, or several that are each useful alone.\012\012In every other respect it behaves like `RemoteEvent`: the values it accepts, who can call which method, and how the authority identifies the sender.";
    unreliableRemoteEventDesc.methods = unreliableRemoteEventMethods;
